cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Agent Cambrian Explosion: From Recursive Self-Improvement to Artificial Agent Ecologies"
message: "If you use this manuscript or its proposed framework, please cite this work and the primary sources relevant to the empirical claim you rely on."
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: "Cheng"
    given-names: "Lu"
    alias: "Jack Lu"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
url: "https://github.com/jklop3841/human"
abstract: >-
  A research book proposing a population-level framework for AI takeoff in which
  environmental inheritance, lineage recursive improvement, low-cost agent
  replication, functional specialization, coordination, and AI-R&D automation
  can jointly produce an Agent Cambrian Explosion and ecological intelligence
  takeoff before or alongside full singleton recursive self-improvement.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - recursive self-improvement
  - lineage recursive improvement
  - agent ecology
  - multi-agent systems
  - digital evolution
  - stigmergy
  - environmental inheritance
  - intelligence explosion
  - AI safety
